# skel-distro.fetch — repos cloned into /etc/skel at prepare time (pinned),
# distro-wide (every build, with or without a profile). Same format as the
# per-profile profiles/<name>/fetch.list: one entry per line.
#
#   <dest-relative-to-skel>   <git-url>   <rev>
#
# Each entry is git-cloned at the pinned <rev>, stripped of its .git, cached
# under .fetch-cache/, and rsync'd into /etc/skel/<dest> AFTER the skel-distro
# overlay and BEFORE any profile layer — so a profile fetch.list line to the
# same dest still wins. Layer order:
#   skel-upstream → skel-distro → skel-distro.fetch → profile
# Bump the <rev> to update; delete a line (or this file) to stop vendoring it —
# the tree disappears from the next build. Fully reversible: the vendored files
# live at distro-owned/unowned skel paths the user can rm -rf, and there is no
# ledger entry (these are static build-time skel files, not runtime mutations).
#
# DESTINATIONS MUST BE DISTRO-OWNED OR UNOWNED SKEL PATHS ONLY.
# Never target an upstream-owned (rsync --delete / install_dir__sync) path —
# upstream's own updater wipes those on `iictl update`. 30-skel.sh fast-fails on
# the prefixes below; the exhaustive collision lint lives in
# tools/lint-additive.sh (issue #8):
#   .config/quickshell  .config/matugen  .config/fish/config.fish
#   .config/fish/functions  .config/zshrc.d  .config/hypr/hyprland
#   .config/fontconfig  .config/starship.toml  .config/hypr/hyprlock.conf
# Safe (unowned) examples: .config/nvim  .antidote  .config/zsh  .tmux/plugins/tpm
#
# Mirrors profiles/username/fetch.list.

# antidote — the zsh plugin manager the themed ~/.zshrc loads (#15, shell layer).
# Vendored to the distro-owned ~/.antidote (a "Safe (unowned)" example above), so
# `iictl update` never wipes it and the guarded `antidote load` in ~/.zshrc works
# fully OFFLINE on a fresh install (no AUR build cost). Pinned to a release tag
# (v2.1.0); bump the rev to update. antidote.zsh sits at the repo root, which is
# exactly what ~/.zshrc sources ($ANTIDOTE_HOME/antidote.zsh).
.antidote   https://github.com/mattmc3/antidote   4913257e0ae3fee2a77e7189e526fe55b6ff9536

